; expect 143
; A binder a TEMPLATE introduces must not capture a name the caller
; passed in. Both places a template can introduce one are exercised,
; because they failed independently and for different reasons.
;
; `addTo`'s template binds `tmp` and then uses the argument. Called
; under a caller's own `tmp`, the emit-time expander substituted the
; argument into a tree where `tmp` was already bound and answered 200 -
; a silent wrong answer, with no diagnostic from either compiler and
; no gate that would have noticed.
;
; `orElse`'s template binds `v` in a match ARM pattern. That one was
; worse than a missed rename: `macroSubstArmsIn` copied the pattern
; verbatim while substituting the body, so the binder stayed and every
; use of it in the body became the ARGUMENT. Measured at 8 - the
; payload - where the caller wrote 42.
;
; 101 + 42 = 143. Under capture the answer is 200 + 8 = 208, so the
; two failures are distinguishable from the pass and from each other.
(data Opt
  (None)
  (Some Int))

(macro (addTo x) (let ((tmp 100))
  (+ tmp x)
))

(macro (orElse o d) (match o
  ((Some v) d)
  ((None) d)
))

(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  (let ((tmp 1))
    (+
      (addTo tmp)      (let ((v 42))
        (orElse (Some 8) v)
      )
    )
  )
)
